  "comparison_contract": "Equivalent spelling comparisons remove only the literal _q3map2_cmdline provenance property from the entity lump, retaining every other entity byte and all other BSP lumps. Preceding-compiler runs use identical decorated arguments and require exact stored BSP lumps, including that provenance. MAP/TGA comparisons use full bytes.",
  "investigations": [
    "Initial Windows/Linux comparison correctly observed differing literal command-line provenance for equivalent spellings. The harness now makes that sole expected metadata difference explicit and separately checks complete raw reference parity. No production output normalization was added."
  ],
  "limits": [
    "The matrix uses generated native Quake III content. It does not claim a fresh complete game/profile or performance qualification.",
    "Only the shared option parsers changed. Legacy positional scale/shift atof parsing, optional source-token/include lookahead and multiline quote accounting remain separate audit tasks.",
    "Existing float narrowing and stage-specific clamping semantics are retained. Strict MAP/script numeric parsing is independent.",
    "The complete new matrix was invoked directly with --reference on all three builds; five related CTest groups also passed on each. The entire 80-group GUI-enabled suite was not rerun.",
    "No editor/game launch, OS input or screen capture, new external code, package refresh or GPU/performance claim. Existing compiler warnings and previously policy-blocked cleanup targets remain."
  ]
